{
  "name": "03-stop-rework-pass-approve-done",
  "description": "A task with one outward action. After the first review passes, the orchestrator's approval job stops the action; the owner returns the task for rework; the builder resubmits, the second review passes, the orchestrator approves, and the free builder gets its fresh lease at once, carries the action out and reports it done.",
  "covers": [
    "PRD Quality requirements, test 8: one trace covers stop, return for rework, pass, approve and done.",
    "PRD Outward actions, steps 2 to 4: action.requested per action, the approval policy as a model check, the immediate fresh lease (action.approved carries lease_seat_id, plan SM-7, SM-8).",
    "PRD Task lifecycle: Stop action (action.stopped, hold.opened action_stopped) through the approval job's result; Return for rework (task.returned_for_rework, criterion.reopened, action.withdrawn, hold.closed); Start action; Report action done, the last one, with task.done.",
    "PRD Event record, command_id: the checks at action.requested are app-originated and carry no key.",
    "PRD Steps and timing: check opens on the action's first queued check, wait_owner follows the action_stopped hold, wait_builder opens at the rework and at the approval, finish opens at the acknowledgement after the approval (plan SM-27)."
  ],
